--TEST--
A group whose children can only wait for each other ends at the deadline, runs no instruction past the wait, and leaves nothing parked that a later send could wake — `rule:concurrency/nothing-is-still-running-when-a-call-returns` and `rule:concurrency/cancellation-runs-no-user-code`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The neighbouring deadline case pins the clock against children that would
// have finished on their own. This is the case where nothing would ever
// finish: two channels, and each child waits for a value only the other could
// send once its own wait had ended. Neither channel is closed, so neither
// `foreach` can end on end-of-stream either.
class Deadlock {
    public static int $reached = 0;
    public static int $past = 0;
}

var $a = new Core\Task\Channel<int>(1);
var $b = new Core\Task\Channel<int>(1);

try {
    Core\Task::all({
        first: fn(): int => {
            Deadlock::$reached += 1;
            foreach ($a as int $n) {
                Deadlock::$past += 1;
                $b->send($n);
            }
            return 1;
        },
        second: fn(): int => {
            Deadlock::$reached += 1;
            foreach ($b as int $n) {
                Deadlock::$past += 1;
                $a->send($n);
            }
            return 2;
        },
    }, {deadline: 100ms});
    echo "the deadlock returned", "\n";
} catch (TimeoutError $e) {
    echo "the deadlock ended at the deadline", "\n";
}

echo Deadlock::$reached, " children waited, ", Deadlock::$past, " ran past the wait", "\n";

// "Leaves no child running", asserted rather than assumed: a child still
// parked on `$a` would be woken by this send and would run the body of its
// `foreach`. The capacity is one and the channel is empty, so the send itself
// does not wait, and the sleep gives any survivor a turn to prove it exists.
$a->send(1);
Core\Time::sleep(20ms);

echo Deadlock::$past, " ran past the wait after the group returned", "\n";
--EXPECT--
the deadlock ended at the deadline
2 children waited, 0 ran past the wait
0 ran past the wait after the group returned
